# Mobile Appium Python Rules

Read **`AGENTS.md`** and **`.cursor/skills/mobile-appium-python/SKILL.md`** before authoring tests.

## Architecture

- Strict imports: `tests → steps → page_actions → page_objects → core`
- Locators only in `src/page_objects/**/*_po.py` under `# --- Locators ---`
- No `driver` in tests or steps
- No page object imports in tests or steps
- No `page_actions` imports in tests when a step exists for the flow

## Code quality

- No `time.sleep()` — use explicit waits from `PageActions` / `BasePage`
- No bare `except:` — use `except Exception:`
- Imports at module top only
- No `pytest.skip()` in page actions
- No secrets in dataproviders — config / encrypted `data/` only

## Tests

- Every UI test: `@pytest.mark.e2e` + priority (`p0`/`p1`/`p2`)
- Allure: epic, feature, story, severity; attach on failure (conftest handles screenshots)
- Re-query elements after navigation — no stale `WebElement` caching across screens
- `@pytest.mark.ignore` excluded from default runs

## App configuration

- `APP_NAME`, `APP_SLUG`, identifiers from `.env` — never hardcode product names
- Platform branching only in page objects
- Sync Appium WebDriver API only
